base_url             REQUIRED  [STRING, HIGH]
  Base URL of the API (without trailing slash)
endpoints            REQUIRED  [LIST, HIGH]
  Endpoint definitions (at least one)
default_rate_limit   optional  [STRING, MEDIUM]
  Max request rate across all endpoints, e.g. "100/s" (count/window; unit s|m|h)
  default: 100/s
schedule             optional  [STRING, MEDIUM]
  Cron expression for recurring runs — the hub scheduler fires it, evaluated in UTC
auth                 optional  [NESTED, MEDIUM]
  Authentication for every endpoint (omit => none)
  kind                 REQUIRED  [STRING, HIGH]
    Authentication method
    one of: bearer, basic, api-key, oauth2, session, none
  username             optional  [STRING, HIGH]
    Username (basic, session)
    required when kind is basic or session
  password_env         optional  [STRING, HIGH]
    Password source: lm secret name, else env var (basic, session)
    required when kind is basic or session
  name                 optional  [STRING, HIGH]
    Header/query parameter name for API key
    required when kind = api-key
  value_env            optional  [STRING, HIGH]
    API key value source: lm secret name, else env var
    required when kind = api-key
  in                   optional  [STRING, MEDIUM]
    Where to place the API key (header|query)
    default: header
  token_env            optional  [STRING, HIGH]
    Bearer token source: lm secret name, else env var (bearer)
  token_value          optional  [STRING, LOW]
    Literal bearer token (dev only — prefer token_env)
  scheme               optional  [STRING, LOW]
    The Authorization header's scheme word (bearer): Bearer by default, Token for Django REST Framework
    default: Bearer
    read only when kind = bearer
    → Bearer (the default), or the word the API expects, e.g. Token for Django REST Framework
  token_url            optional  [STRING, HIGH]
    OAuth2 token endpoint (client-credentials grant)
    required when kind = oauth2
    read only when kind = oauth2
  client_id            optional  [STRING, HIGH]
    OAuth2 client id
    required when kind = oauth2
    read only when kind = oauth2
  client_secret_env    optional  [STRING, HIGH]
    OAuth2 client secret source: lm secret name, else env var
    required when kind = oauth2
    read only when kind = oauth2
  scope                optional  [STRING, MEDIUM]
    OAuth2 scope, space-separated
    read only when kind = oauth2
  client_auth          optional  [STRING, LOW]
    How the OAuth2 client authenticates to the token endpoint (basic | post)
    default: basic
    read only when kind = oauth2
    one of: basic, post
    → basic (the default) sends the client id and secret as HTTP Basic; post puts them in the body
  login_url            optional  [STRING, HIGH]
    Where the login form posts: Spring Security's /login, the container's j_security_check
    required when kind = session
    read only when kind = session
  prime_url            optional  [STRING, MEDIUM]
    The page GET first, for the session cookie and the CSRF token; login_url by default
    read only when kind = session
  username_field       optional  [STRING, LOW]
    The form's username field (j_username for the container's login)
    default: username
    read only when kind = session
  password_field       optional  [STRING, LOW]
    The form's password field (j_password for the container's login)
    default: password
    read only when kind = session
  csrf_field           optional  [STRING, MEDIUM]
    The hidden input carrying the CSRF token in the primed page (_csrf under Spring Security)
    read only when kind = session
  at least one of token_env, token_value when kind is bearer
    → Use `lm secret set <NAME> ...` then reference via token_env: <NAME>
tls                  optional  [NESTED, MEDIUM]
  Trust an internal CA for every endpoint: {ca_secret: the lm secret holding its PEM certificate(s)}
  ca_secret            REQUIRED  [STRING, HIGH]
    Name of the lm secret holding the CA's PEM certificate(s); only those CAs are trusted
http_version         optional  [STRING, LOW]
  HTTP version every request asks for: "1.1" or "2" (omit => negotiated, HTTP/2 when the server offers it)
headers              optional  [LIST, MEDIUM]
  Static headers sent on every request, [{name, value | value_env}]
  → headers is a list of { name, value|value_env } objects
defaults             optional  [NESTED, LOW]
  Per-endpoint defaults merged into each endpoint
  kind                 optional  [STRING, LOW]
    Not accepted in spec.defaults — refused by validation; declare it on each endpoint
  query                optional  [STRING, LOW]
    Not accepted in spec.defaults — refused by validation; declare it on each endpoint
  base_url             optional  [STRING, LOW]
    Not accepted in spec.defaults — refused by validation; declare it at spec.base_url
  auth                 optional  [NESTED, LOW]
    Not accepted in spec.defaults — refused by validation; declare it at spec.auth
  tls                  optional  [NESTED, LOW]
    Not accepted in spec.defaults — refused by validation; declare it at spec.tls
  http_version         optional  [STRING, LOW]
    Not accepted in spec.defaults — refused by validation; declare it at spec.http_version
  default_rate_limit   optional  [STRING, LOW]
    Not accepted in spec.defaults — refused by validation; declare it at spec.default_rate_limit
  graphql_path         optional  [STRING, LOW]
    Not accepted in spec.defaults — refused by validation; declare it at spec.graphql_path
  mapping              optional  [NESTED, LOW]
    Not accepted here — refused by validation; declare the mapping on its endpoint
  response_format      optional  [STRING, MEDIUM]
    What the answer is: json (the default) or xml — attributes under @, text beside them under #text
    default: json
    one of: json, xml
  incremental          optional  [NESTED, MEDIUM]
    Incremental strategy (mode full | watermark; defaults to full)
    → incremental is a block, not a scalar: incremental: { mode: watermark, param: ..., watermark_path: ... }
  headers              optional  [LIST, LOW]
    Not accepted here — refused by validation; declare headers at spec.headers
    → Move the headers block up to spec.headers (connector level)
  variables            optional  [NESTED, LOW]
    Static variables sent with every request; the relay cursor is injected on top
  header               optional  [STRING, LOW]
    The SOAP header template (inner <Header> content; same placeholders as body)
  soap_action          optional  [STRING, LOW]
    Sent as the SOAPAction header (an empty quoted string when absent)
graphql_path         optional  [STRING, LOW]
  Path appended to base_url for GraphQL endpoints
  default: /graphql
window               optional  [STRING, MEDIUM]
  Fence scheduled runs to a UTC time window, HH:MM-HH:MM (a manual run bypasses it)
mapping              optional  [NESTED, LOW]
  Not accepted here — refused by validation; declare the mapping on its endpoint
